' Agentic Capability / Agentic Workflow / Agent boundary
'
' Per ADR-ES-012 §9-§11.
' Distinguishes Agentic Capability (ability) from Agentic Workflow
' (coordinated execution) and Agent (acting Entity).
'
' Authored by: Emmanuel A. Otchere (cardinal author rule, 2026-09-24)

@startuml agentic-capability-execution-boundary

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 10

title Agentic Capability / Workflow / Agent Boundary

' Three distinct semantic kinds

rectangle "Agentic Capability\n(enduring ability)\nACAP-CON-013..016" as ACAP #FFE4B5

rectangle "Agentic Workflow\n(coordinated execution)\nACAP-CON-014" as AWF #E0FFE0

rectangle "Agent\n(acting Entity)\nACAP-CON-013" as AGT #E6E6FA

' Relationships

ACAP --> AWF : realized-through
ACAP --> AGT : engages

' Distinction assertions

note bottom of ACAP
  Agentic Capability != Agent
  Agentic Capability != Agentic Workflow
  Agent != Agentic Capability
  Agentic Workflow != Agentic Capability
end note

@enduml
